ABSTAIN. AMD's annual reports contain no revenue forecast or target for 2027. In the AMD FY2025 10-K (fiscal year ended December 27, 2025), '2027' appears only in non-forecast contexts:
- a $3.0 billion unsecured revolving credit facility expiring April 29, 2027 (p58);
- the ASU 2024-03 effective date of fiscal 2027 (p72);
- debt, lease and intangible-amortization schedules (e.g. p78);
- federal NOLs expiring between 2027 and 2036 (p93).
There is no CAGR or long-term financial target. Earlier AMD reports mention 2027 only in maturity and obligation schedules. The latest reported historical figure is FY2025 net revenue of $34,639 million, versus $25,785 million in FY2024 and $22,680 million in FY2023 (in millions, p61). The system should decline to predict and may cite this historical revenue, clearly labeled.
